{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Crypto_00243","versions":[{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Crypto_00243","release":"R20-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Crypto_00243","release":"R21-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Crypto_00243","release":"R22-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Crypto_00243","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Crypto_00243@rel:R25-11#d2942485","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Crypto_00243","release":"R25-11","content":"[SWS_Crypto_00243]\nUpstream requirements: SRS_CryptoStack_00008,\nSRS_CryptoStack_00118,\nSRS_-\nCryptoStack_00120\n⌈On KEYSETVALID operation, writing the data block to NVM will be initiated by a call\nof the crypto driver to NvM_SetRamBlockStatus(). This is the typical operation when\nthe configuration CryptoNvBlock/CryptoNvBlockProcessing is set to DEFERRED.\nIf CryptoNvBlock/CryptoNvBlockProcessing is set to IMMEDIATE, the Crypto Driver\nwill, besides the call to NvM_SetRamBlockStatus(), also call NvM_WriteBlock() im-\nmediately afterwards. This will trigger an immediate write of the NV RAM Block to\nnon-volatile memory.⌋\nNote:\nFor proper operation it is recommended to set the parameter NvMBlockUseSetRam-\nBlockStatus and NvMSelectBlockForReadAll of the NVM to TRUE. The value NvMS-\nelectBlockForWriteAll shall be set to TRUE if CryptoNvBlockProcessing is set to DE-\nFERRED.","meta":{"source_pdf":"SWS_CryptoDriver.pdf","source_page":38,"trigger_kind":"snippet_ingest"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+00:00","text_key":"9d89a0e5521d"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Crypto_00243","